{"id": "EUVD-2026-107239", "enisaUuid": "d905545b-abae-3cb2-affb-f7fa6d2de783", "description": "Trudesk through 1.2.11 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows authenticated users to read tickets outside their groups via GET /api/v1/tickets/:uid. Attackers can enumerate sequential ticket uids to read every ticket's subject, issue, comments, owner and assignee, because the apiTickets.single handler skips group membership checks.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T12:39:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:48", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/multiple-vuln-trudesk-1211", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/controllers/api/v1/tickets.js#L721-L740", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/trudesk-through-1.2.11-authorization-bypass-via-get-api-v1-tickets-uid"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114392", "GHSA-836q-x8w9-9gg6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "40498ecd-0347-37df-bca8-bb51ae8479c0", "product": {"name": "trudesk", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "663e10b1-6db8-31f6-8efa-51cf6ba504c4", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}], "isExploited": false}